\label{rmk: action currents on ground states}
The ground states satisfy the relations
\begin{align*}
    \boldsymbol{\chi}_{0}\boldsymbol{\upomega}
    \, = \,
    -\boldsymbol{\upxi}\,,
    \mspace{150mu} 
    \boldsymbol{\eta}_{0}\boldsymbol{\upomega}
    \, = \,&\,
    -\boldsymbol{\uptheta}\,,
    \phantom{\Big\vert}
    \\
    \boldsymbol{\chi}_{0}\boldsymbol{\uptheta}
    \, = \,
    \mathbf{1}\,,
    \mspace{65mu}
    \text{ and }
    \mspace{66mu}
    \boldsymbol{\eta}_{0}\boldsymbol{\upxi}
    \, = \,&\,
    -\mathbf{1}\,.
    \phantom{\Big\vert}
\end{align*}
Let us explicitly write down the computation for the first of these relations.
We have, for a sufficiently large corner contour~$\gamma$ encircling the origin,
\begin{align*}
    \boldsymbol{\chi}_{0}\boldsymbol{\upomega}
    \, = \, & \,
    \sqint^{\sharp}_{\gamma}
    \frac{\textnormal{d}^{\sharp}\mathbf{u}}{2\pi \mathbbm{i}}\,
    \mathbf{u}^{[0]}_\diamond\,
    \boldsymbol{\upchi}(\mathbf{u}_\textnormal{m}) \cdot 
    \Big(-\boldsymbol\upxi(0)\boldsymbol\uptheta(0)\Big)
    + \textnormal{\small Null}
    \\
    \, = \, & \,
    -\frac{1}{2\pi}
    \sum_{\mathbf{u}_\diamond\in\textnormal{int}_\diamond\gamma}
    \partial_\sharp\boldsymbol{\upchi}(\mathbf{u}_\diamond)\boldsymbol\upxi(0)\boldsymbol\uptheta(0)
    + \textnormal{\small Null}
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
    \, = \, & \,
    -\frac{1}{4\pi}
    \sum_{\mathbf{u}_\bullet\in\textnormal{int}_\bullet\gamma}
    \Delta_\sharp\boldsymbol\upxi(\mathbf{u}_\bullet)\boldsymbol\upxi(0)\boldsymbol\uptheta(0)
    + \textnormal{\small Null}
    \\
    \, = \, & \,
    -\frac{1}{4\pi}
    \sum_{\mathbf{u}_\bullet\in\textnormal{int}_\bullet\gamma}
    4\pi\delta_{0,\mathbf{u}_\bullet}\boldsymbol\upxi(0)
    + \textnormal{\small Null}
    \\
    \, = \, & \,
    -\boldsymbol\upxi(0)
    + \textnormal{\small Null}\phantom{\Big\vert}
    \\
    \, = \, & \,
    -\boldsymbol{\upxi}\,,\phantom{\Big\vert}
\end{align*}
where we have used the discrete Stokes' formula ---Section~\ref{subsubsec: discrete integration}---, the factorisation of the discrete Laplacian operator ---Remark~\ref{rmk: factorisation laplacian}---, and the null field from Example~\ref{ex: cubic null field}.
\hfill$\diamond$

With a simple application of the discrete Stokes' formula and the discrete monomials value $0^{[k]}=0$ for $k>0$ ---Section~\ref{subsubsec: discrete monomials}---, one can check that all four ground states ($\mathbf{1}$, $\boldsymbol{\upxi}$, $\boldsymbol{\uptheta}$, and $\boldsymbol{\upomega}$) are annihilated by the current modes with positive index.
That is, we have
\begin{align*}
    \boldsymbol{\chi}_{k}\boldsymbol{\upomega}
    \,=\,

    \mathrlap{\hspace{0pt}\overline{\scalebox{1}[1]{\phantom{\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\chi}}}}}}\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\chi}}
_{k}\boldsymbol{\upomega}
    \, = \,
    \boldsymbol{\eta}_{k}\boldsymbol{\upomega}
    \,=\,

    \mathrlap{\hspace{0pt}\overline{\scalebox{1}[1]{\phantom{\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\eta}}}}}}\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\eta}}
_{k}\boldsymbol{\upomega}
    \, = \, 0\,,
\end{align*}
and similarly for $\mathbf{1}$, $\boldsymbol{\upxi}$, and $\boldsymbol{\uptheta}$\,.
\hfill $\diamond$

